{"at":"2026-10-13T11:25:39.161Z","tool":"open_session","args":"{\"issue\":11404,\"questions\":\"1. **Which of the three proposed options ships?** The issue offers: an Italic option in the panel, Ctrl+I / Cmd+I, or an italic font. *Suggested:* an \\\"Italic\\\" toggle in the properties panel **and** Ctrl+I (Cmd+I on macOS); no separate italic font in the font list.\\n2. *","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T11:26:02.907Z","tool":"record_answers","args":"{\"issue\":11404,\"answers\":\"1. (user) A panel toggle and Ctrl/Cmd+I; one italic property per text element, no separate italic font.\\n2. (user) Italic applies to the whole text element only; there is no partial italic. Bold is out of scope.\\n3. (accepted suggestion) An \\\"Italic\\\" toggle next to the tex","outcome":"ok"}
